module lib/hf/uhf
  Unrestricted Hartree-Fock (UHF), checked against PySCF 2.5.0.

  When a molecule has more electrons of one spin than the other, the two spins
  feel different fields, because exchange acts only between electrons of the
  same spin. UHF gives each spin its own density and its own Fock matrix,

      F_a = H + J(Da + Db) - K(Da)
      F_b = H + J(Da + Db) - K(Db)

  so both spins feel the Coulomb field of every electron, and each feels
  exchange only with its own spin. The loop is lib/hf/scf_loop's with two
  densities; this module holds the UHF checks.

  The price of the freedom: a UHF wavefunction is in general not a state of
  definite total spin. The result records `<S^2>`, and its excess over the
  exact value measures the spin contamination.
